            "correct_answer": null,
            "solution_explanation": "The correct answer is B. This question relates to Standard V(B) Communication \nwith Clients and Prospective Clients. Scott has issued a research report stating \nthat he expects the price of Walkton Industries stock to rise by US$8 a share \n\"because the dividend will increase\" by US$1.50 per share. He has made this \nstatement knowing that the dividend will increase only if Congress enacts certain \nlegislation, an uncertain prospect. By stating that the dividend will increase, Scott \nfailed to separate fact from opinion. The information regarding passage of legisla­\ntion is not material nonpublic information because it is conjecture, and the ques­\ntion does not state whether the US representative gave Scott her opinion on the \npassage of the legislation in confidence. She could have been offering this opinion \nto anyone who asked. Therefore, answer A is incorrect. It may be acceptable to \nbase a recommendation, in part, on an expectation of future events, even though \nthey may be uncertain. Therefore, answer C is incorrect. \nSee Standard V(B): Communication with Clients and Prospective Clients"
