            "solution_explanation": "The correct answer is B. Standard VI(B) Priority of Transactions does not limit \ntransactions of company employees that differ from current recommendations as \nlong as the sale does not disadvantage current clients. Thus, answer A is incor­\nrect. Answer C is incorrect because the Standard does not require the matching \nof personal and client trades. \nSee Standard VI(B): Priority of Transactions"
