            "solution_explanation": "B is correct. Non-cash benefits refer to the convenience yield, which causes a \npreference for owning the physical commodity rather than a derivative contract. \nA is incorrect in that derivatives provide price transparency while the market for \nphysical commodities is much less transparent. C is incorrect in that the more \nfrequent trading of derivatives on organized exchanges enhances liquidity while \nphysical commodity markets are characterized by infrequent trading and thus \npoor liquidity."
