            "solution_explanation": "The correct answer is B. The debtholder payoff has deteriorated versus the share­\nholders, because they are effectively short a put option on the value of the firm \nequal to the value of debt, which has appreciated in value.\nThe debtholder payoff is min(D, VT) = D - max(0, D - VT) and equals the debt \nface value (D) minus a put option on firm value (VT) with an exercise price of D. \nAnswer A is incorrect because the debtholders, not the shareholders, have sold \na put option. C is incorrect, because the shareholders own a call option, but it is \nnot sold by the debtholders."
