            "q_num": 1,
            "stem": "Which one of the following statements most correctly describes a positively \nskewed distribution of P/E multiples?",
            "options": {
              "A": "The average P/E is greater than the median P/E.",
              "B": "The distribution includes firms with negative EPS.",
              "C": "The average P/E more likely reflects the distribution's central tendency."
            },
            "correct_answer": "A",
            "solution_explanation": "A is correct because the mean (i.e., average) P/E exceeds the median P/E in a pos­\nitively skewed distribution since the average is affected by the presence of very \nhigh P/E multiples that may be outliers within the distribution.\nB is incorrect because P/E multiples are not economically meaningful and are \ntypically not included in the distribution.\nC is incorrect because the median is a more likely reflection of the distribution's \ncentral tendency when the distribution is positively skewed."
