            "stem": "An analyst analyzes StevCo's observed value-to-book multiple of 1.60 based on \nthe following information:\n\t\n■\nStevCo's WACC is 7.5%, and its long-run growth of FCFF is 3.0%.\n\t\n■\nStevCo's book value of equity is EUR400 million, and its book value of debt \nis EUR900 million.\n\t\n■\nStevCo's base-year (t = 0) EBITDA is equal to EUR300 million, and its \ndepreciation expense is EUR150 million. The company spends EUR190 mil­\nlion on capital expenditures. StevCo operates with zero net working capital. \nStevCo's tax rate is 30%.\nWhich one of the following is closest to the analyst's estimate of StevCo's justified \nvalue-to-book multiple assuming constant growth?",
