            "solution_explanation": "C is correct. Choice C is correct because the increase in assumed dividend \npayout ratio for Years 3 and 4 causes assumed dividends per share to grow more \nrapidly than EPS during those two years.\nChoice A is incorrect because the dividend payout ratio remains at 40% for both \nyears, so EPS and dividends per share are assumed to grow at the same rate in \nthose two years.\nChoice B is incorrect because the dividend payout ratio remains at 40% in Year 2 \nbefore increasing in Year 3. As a result, EPS and dividends per share grow at the \nsame rate in Year 2."
