            "stem": "Fairplay reported the information shown in Exhibit 1 related to the sale of its \nproducts during 2009, which was its first year of business:\nExhibit 1: Fairplay \nRevenue\nUSD1,000,000\nReturns of goods sold\nUSD100,000\nCash collected\nUSD800,000\nCost of goods sold\nUSD700,000\nUnder the accrual basis of accounting, how much net revenue would be reported \non Fairplay's 2009 income statement?",
            "options": {
              "A": "USD200,000",
              "B": "USD900,000",
              "C": "USD1,000,000"
            },
            "correct_answer": "B",
            "solution_explanation": "B is correct. Net revenue is revenue for goods sold during the period less any \nreturns and allowances, or USD1,000,000 minus USD100,000 = USD900,000."
