            "solution_explanation": "A is correct. The quick ratio is defined as:\n\tQuick ratio  =   Cash + Short-term marketable instruments + Receivables \n \n \n \n________________________________________ \n \n \nCurrent liabilities    \nThe quick ratio for each issuer is:\n\tIssuer A quick ratio  =   100 + 20 + 300 \n \n___________ \n400 + 40  =  420 \n_ \n440\n  = 0.9545\n\tIssuer B quick ratio  =   120 + 10 + 300 \n \n___________ \n500 + 20  =  430 \n_ \n520\n  = 0.8269\n\tIssuer C quick ratio  =   50 + 20 + 200 \n_ \n300 + 0  =  270 \n_ \n300\n  = 0.9000"
