        "html_content": "\n                <h1>Fiscal Policy</h1>\n                <div class=\"module-meta-banner\">\n                    <span class=\"meta-tag\">Economics</span>\n                    <span class=\"meta-tag\">Learning Module 3</span>\n                    <span class=\"meta-tag\">Trang sách: 87</span>\n                </div>\n                <h2>Learning Outcome Statements (LOS)</h2>\n                <blockquote>\n                    <p>The candidate should be able to master the following concepts according to the CFA Institute Curriculum:</p>\n                </blockquote>\n                <ul class=\"los-list-styled\">\n                    <li>compare monetary and fiscal policy</li><li>describe roles and objectives of fiscal policy as well as arguments as</li><li>to whether the size of a national debt relative to GDP matters</li><li>describe tools of fiscal policy, including their advantages and</li><li>disadvantages</li><li>explain the implementation of fiscal policy and difficulties of</li><li>implementation as well as whether a fiscal policy is expansionary or</li><li>contractionary</li>\n                </ul>\n                <div class=\"note-box\">\n                    <p><strong>CFA Exam Focus:</strong> Hãy đọc kỹ các mục tiêu học tập (LOS) bên trên, sau đó thực hành bộ câu hỏi trắc nghiệm bên dưới. Toàn bộ câu hỏi được trích xuất 100% nguyên bản từ giáo trình chuẩn 2027 kèm lời giải thích chi tiết của Viện CFA.</p>\n                </div>\n                ",
        "total_questions": 5,
        "practice_problems": [
          {
            "q_num": 1,
            "stem": "Crowding out refers to a:",
            "options": {
              "A": "fall in interest rates that reduces private investment.",
              "B": "rise in private investment that reduces private consumption.",
              "C": "rise in government borrowing that reduces the ability of the private sector \nto access investment funds."
            },
            "correct_answer": "C",
            "solution_explanation": "C is correct. A fall in interest rates is likely to lead to a rise in investment. Crowd­\ning out refers to government borrowing that reduces the ability of the private \nsector to invest."
          },
          {
            "q_num": 2,
            "stem": "A contractionary fiscal policy will always involve which of the following?",
            "options": {
              "A": "Balanced budget",
              "B": "Reduction in government spending",
              "C": "Fall in the budget deficit or rise in the surplus"
            },
            "correct_answer": "C",
            "solution_explanation": "C is correct. Note that a reduction in government spending could be accompa­\nnied by an even bigger fall in taxation, making it be expansionary."
          },
          {
            "q_num": 3,
            "stem": "Which one of the following statements is most accurate?",
            "options": {
              "A": "Ricardian equivalence refers to individuals having no idea of future tax \nliabilities.",
              "B": "Governments do not allow political pressures to influence fiscal policies but \ndo allow voters to affect monetary policies.",
              "C": "If there is high unemployment in an economy, then easy monetary and fiscal \npolicies should lead to an expansion in aggregate demand."
            },
            "correct_answer": "C",
            "solution_explanation": "C is correct. Note that governments often allow pressure groups to affect fiscal \npolicy and that Ricardian equivalence involves individuals correctly anticipating \nfuture taxes. Thus, A and B are not correct choices."
          },
          {
            "q_num": 4,
            "stem": "Which statement regarding fiscal policy is most accurate?",
            "options": {
              "A": "Cyclically adjusted budget deficits are appropriate indicators of fiscal policy.",
              "B": "To raise business capital spending, personal income taxes should be \nreduced.",
              "C": "An increase in the budget surplus is associated with expansionary fiscal \npolicy."
            },
            "correct_answer": "A",
            "solution_explanation": "A is correct. Cyclically adjusted budget deficits are appropriate indicators of fiscal \npolicy. These are defined as the deficit that would exist if the economy was at full \nemployment (or full potential output)."
          },
          {
            "q_num": 5,
            "stem": "The least likely explanation for why fiscal policy cannot stabilize aggregate de­\nmand completely is that:",
            "options": {
              "A": "private sector behavior changes over time.",
              "B": "policy changes are implemented very quickly.",
              "C": "fiscal policy focuses more on inflation than on unemployment."
            },
            "correct_answer": "B",
            "solution_explanation": "B is correct. Fiscal policy is subject to recognition, action, and impact lags."
          }
        ]
