            "correct_answer": null,
            "solution_explanation": "The correct answer is A. The null hypothesis, H 0, is that the variances are equal \nbefore and after the change in rules:\n\nSolutions\n377\n\tH 0 : σ Before \n2    =  σ After \n2 .\n\tH a : σ Before \n2    ≠  σ After \n2 .\nTo test this hypothesis, an F-test is used. The F-statistic is calculated as\n\tF  =   \ns\n 1 2 \n_ \ns\n 2 2\n   =   22.367 \n_ \n15.795\n   =  1.416.\nTherefore, the analyst should fail to reject the null hypothesis because the calcu­\nlated F-test statistic, 1.416, is within the range of the two critical values.\nB is incorrect: The analyst should fail to reject the null hypothesis because the \ncalculated F-test statistic, 1.416, is within the range of the two critical values.\nC is incorrect: Hypothesis testing involves rejecting or failing to reject the null \nhypothesis, not rejecting or failing to reject the alternative hypothesis."
