            "solution_explanation": "The correct response is B. Historical simulation offers tractability-allowing for \nstatements such as \"The portfolio would lose $X if the markets moved like they \ndid on 16 July 2024.\" Therefore, results from historical simulation are generally \nsimple and straightforward to explain to wide audiences.\nA is incorrect: Historical simulation is hypersensitive to the quality of historical \ndata because it is central to the analyses.\nC is incorrect: Unlike historical simulation, Monte Carlo simulation offers \ntremendous flexibility in distributional assumptions, correlations, and so on, to \nrespond to evolving market conditions. For example, the decision could be made \nto increase volatility across the board if markets are believed to have become \nmore volatile."
