            "solution_explanation": "The correct response is C. Bootstrapping involves generating random samples \nfrom a given dataset, whose distribution serves as a proxy for the real underlying \ndistribution.\nA is incorrect: Bootstrapping does not generate new data points or fill in missing \ndata points.\nB is incorrect: Bootstrapping involves generating random samples from a given \ndataset, whose distribution serves as a proxy for the real underlying distribution. \nAny biases in the original dataset can be expected to carry over to the bootstrap­\nping samples."
